WebAuthnSessionValidator::validateSignatureWithData
├── given a valid software-P256 credential + assertion over the challenge
│   ├── when user-verification is required (UV bit set)
│   │   └── it should return true
│   └── when user-verification is not required
│       └── it should return true (the UV bit is present anyway)
├── given a valid credential but a mismatched challenge
│   └── it should return false (the challenge binds the digest)
├── given an all-zero pubkey (the empty sentinel)
│   └── when any signature is checked
│       └── it should return false (early return before verify)
├── given a half-zero pubkey (x or y == 0, a degenerate credential)
│   ├── when y == 0
│   │   └── it should return false (rejected by the OR guard, mirroring onInstall)
│   ├── when x == 0
│   │   └── it should return false (rejected by the OR guard)
│   └── when the signature blob is undecodable
│       └── it should return false (the OR guard short-circuits before signature decode)
├── given a real pubkey + a well-formed but invalid WebAuthnAuth
│   └── it should return false (verification fails, no revert)
├── when the signature blob is not decodable as a WebAuthnAuth
│   └── it should revert (abi.decode of garbage)
└── when the credential blob is not decodable as (x, y, requireUV)
    └── it should revert (abi.decode of garbage)
